{"id": "EUVD-2026-105165", "enisaUuid": "ed3082ae-457c-3d02-8754-349b81022b0b", "description": "Modoboa before 2.8.0 contains an insecure direct object reference vulnerability that allows authenticated users to create auto-reply messages for arbitrary mailboxes by supplying another user's mbox value. Attackers can POST to /api/v2/armessages/ to inject attacker-controlled auto-reply subject and content into victims' settings or break their auto-reply management via MultipleObjectsReturned errors.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T15:40:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T16:19:21", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/modoboa/modoboa/issues/3945", "https://github.com/modoboa/modoboa/commit/e0a4e3b9ee8ad84dba46e4c0f04cbbe7cf78c38d", "https://github.com/modoboa/modoboa/releases/tag/2.8.0", "https://github.com/modoboa/modoboa/blob/2.7.2/modoboa/autoreply/api/v2/serializers.py", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/modoboa-before-2.8.0-idor-via-api-v2-armessages-auto-reply-creation"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-113599", "GHSA-rg3x-36vj-2j2w"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.34, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ce4b7e7d-1dd9-3273-91f6-9c9633a2d3cc", "product": {"name": "modoboa", "vendor": {"name": "modoboa"}}, "product_version": "0 <2.8.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8a8f1dd6-848d-338c-b542-9849ceea98e3", "vendor": {"name": "modoboa"}}], "isExploited": false}